diff -ruN pa/repo/ports/doomdmc/README.txt pb/repo/ports/doomdmc/README.txt
--- pa/repo/ports/doomdmc/README.txt	2026-11-03 18:55:16
+++ pb/repo/ports/doomdmc/README.txt	2026-11-03 19:55:15
@@ -17,3 +17,11 @@
 Cost work: -O2 (was -Oz), fastfix.c (FixedDiv via divu, bit-exact), qimg.c (extent run cache, no stats on the
   line-fill path), qsolid.c (repeat plan-D floor/ceiling columns copied), and the main loop skips the redraw of
   a frame that follows no tic (virtual time makes every other TryRunTics call tic-less).
+Baked E1M1 hot set (disk-request cut, data ROM): ports/doomdmc/bake_e1m1.txt lists 4-byte units of the logical image
+  (E1 pack) that build.sh cuts out of the NOR image (tools/bake_map.py -> bakemap.c, qbake.c looks them up). Reads of
+  them (record cache fills and rec_* reads, img_read / img_read_async, the direct column read) are copied from ROM, no
+  disk request; the bake is enabled only if the image's header CRC matches (else everything goes to the disk as before).
+  Block list = tools/bake_select.py over REQLOG files of unbaked runs of several E1M1 walks (tools/bake_route.sh R nb;
+  routes in doomd_main.c Q_ROUTE), sized to fill the data ROM (BUDGET 91700 for the current rodata; the link fails with
+  "will not fit in region DROM" when rodata grows, lower the budget). tools/bake_eval.py scores a list on other logs.
+  NOBAKE=1 builds without; BAKE_IMG / BAKE_RANGES override the image / list.
